       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. Higher doses add significantly more peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, with little extra blood pressure benefit.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the maximum standard dose.\n- **Enter 10 mg now and add a second agent** if the goal is more blood pressure control. An ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic is a common choice.\n- **Enter 20 mg as written.** I can do this if you confirm the dose is intentional. A note on the order with the rationale would help pharmacy and nursing.\n\nWhich would you like?"
